# BFF Aggregator Pattern

## Async & parallel aggregation

- Java 21 Virtual Threads only — `Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()`
- BFF parallel calls: `CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(..., virtualExecutor)` + `.thenCombine()`
- No platform threads, no `RestTemplate` — use `WebClient` or `RestClient` with connect/read/write timeouts

```java
// ✅ BFF fork + merge
var staticFuture = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> staticData.load(ids), virtualExecutor);
var dynamicFuture = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> inventoryClient.getStock(skus), virtualExecutor);
return staticFuture.thenCombine(dynamicFuture, this::merge).join();
```

## External client wrappers

Every external API method in a Client Wrapper **must** have:

```java
@CircuitBreaker(name = "inventoryService", fallbackMethod = "getStockFallback")
public Map<String, Integer> getStock(Collection<String> skus) { ... }

private Map<String, Integer> getStockFallback(Collection<String> skus, Throwable t) {
    return Collections.emptyMap(); // safe default — never throw
}
```

Fallback signature = same params + `Throwable`. Return empty/default data so BFF stays alive.

## Platform config

`application.yml` must include `spring.threads.virtual.enabled: true` and Resilience4j circuit breaker instances per backend service.
